From: FORZA-LAUNCHER-FOR-MAC-BLACKWELL-PROJECT
Subject: [PATCH] streaming: a download that did not happen exits with a failure

MetalHorizon 2.0.0. `xodus-cli streaming` gave up without the game (not enough free disk space, no licence, an
unexpected content key) after printing why, and still exited with success: MetalHorizon said "Download finished.",
Download the Game stayed, and there was no game (report of 21 November: 171 GB needed, 16 GB free, after the
package's index, about 1 GB, had been fetched). run_reader now says whether the files were downloaded, and `run` exits
with a failure when they were not. The index cached for that run (.xodus-streaming-tmp.msixvc, about 1 GB, emptied by
the next run anyway) is removed when the download is given up, so it does not hold room on a disk short of it.

On top of 0006, in the tree MetalHorizon bundles xodus-cli from (work/xodus), with patch -p1.
Tests: cargo test --release --offline -p xodus-cli streaming.
